              <p class="research-desc">
                A Ruby on Rails API that stores and retrieves blobs through one interface backed by four
                interchangeable storage backends — S3-compatible object storage, a database table, the local
                filesystem, or FTP. The centerpiece is a <strong>from-scratch implementation of AWS Signature
                  Version 4</strong>: the S3 backend speaks the S3 REST protocol directly over <code>Net::HTTP</code> with no AWS or S3 libraries anywhere, and the signer is validated byte-for-byte against AWS's
                officially documented example signature. Backends sit behind a clean adapter pattern resolved by a
                config-driven factory, so adding one touches a single class. <strong>34 tests</strong> across unit
                and integration layers, CI on every push, and a Docker Compose setup that runs it against a real
